--- !u!114 &1842857910
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 1842857907}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f7e0f95304b6c9f4397e206d40e8bdbd, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  dialogueLines:
  - speaker: Blue
    text: I am curious, why would someone like you choose a company like Black Hole
      Industries? It sounds to me that they value efficiency and speed over creative
      expression. You do not seem like someone who would simply attempt to finish
      tasks as fast as possible without so much as an afterthought.
  - speaker: Mars
    text: "I didn\u2019t CHOOSE to join Black Hole. They had positions open, I applied,
      got selected, simple as that. This job is just a trial run to see what my strengths
      are."
  - speaker: Blue
    text: You used to be someone quite creative. An actor, a writer perhaps?
  - speaker: Mars
    text: "\u2026I used to. But that\u2019s in the past. Acting might be fulfilling,
      but it doesn\u2019t pay the bills like it did during the 21st century."
  - speaker: Blue
    text: And you are any better out here? Carrying useless equipment through ice
      and snow for people who do not even know your name? For people who force you
      to become a number and hide your humanity?
  - speaker: Mars
    text: "Better than scavenging between gigs while everyone told me acting isn\u2019t
      a \u201Creal\u201D job. At least here, I\u2019m useful. I have value."
  - speaker: Blue
    text: Was it actually value though? Or was simply fear of judgement from people
      who you believed were your betters?
  - speaker: Mars
    text: .....
  - speaker: Blue
    text: When you mentioned acting, your eyes ignited like someone with true passion.
      Did it feel right? Did it make you happy, despite the circumstances?
  - speaker: Mars
    text: ..........
