--- !u!114 &2010066226
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 2010066223}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: f7e0f95304b6c9f4397e206d40e8bdbd, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  dialogueLines:
  - speaker: Mars
    text: "\u201CThere\u2019s an old folktale from the days before humanity took
      to the stars that really puts into perspective how we\u2019ve never changed,
      even if we think we have. Just because we have spaceships and lightspeed engines,
      it doesn\u2019t mean we ourselves have changed. Think of technology as the
      face humanity wears to hide and deny our animalistic origins\u2026\r\nThe story
      goes that a climber believed the mountain by his town would forgive him if
      he just explained himself clearly enough. You see, an avalanche had buried
      much of the town, and the climber blamed himself because he dared to demolish
      parts of the mountain for new buildings. The climber eventually reached the
      summit after much hardship and strife. There, he began speaking.\r\nBut the
      mountain does not listen. The mountain does not care that you have to feed
      your family. The mountain does not care that you are smaller and weaker than
      it. The mountain only knows actions and consequences. It only remembers what
      was left behind.\r\nBut the climber kept speaking anyway, doomed to eternally
      explain and justify to the complete indifference of the mountain itself.\r"
